00:56:41.820 --> 00:56:43.300
on top of the leaderboard.

00:56:43.640 --> 00:56:45.400
48-year-old Arnold Palmer,

00:56:45.680 --> 00:56:47.520
who has not won a tournament in this country

00:56:47.520 --> 00:56:49.960
since 1973, leads

00:56:49.960 --> 00:56:51.900
at 7-under, one ahead

00:56:51.900 --> 00:56:53.460
of Stadler and Weiskopf.

00:56:53.740 --> 00:56:56.080
He had a 20-foot birdie putt on 15

00:56:56.080 --> 00:56:58.160
to try and increase his lead.

00:57:02.620 --> 00:57:06.260
Arnold had yet another 20-foot-plus putt for birdie.

00:57:12.030 --> 00:57:15.150
So after missing two birdie putts on 15 and 16,

00:57:15.550 --> 00:57:19.170
Arnie went to a three-iron to get close on the far 317.

00:57:33.610 --> 00:57:38.610
And so for the third consecutive hole, Arnold Palmer had a birdie putt to increase his lead.

00:57:40.050 --> 00:57:42.290
For the third time, he was denied.

00:57:42.990 --> 00:57:46.010
The 18th with pure Palmer at his best.

00:57:46.910 --> 00:57:48.390
First, a crashing drive.

00:58:00.440 --> 00:58:05.190
Then it was a seven iron hurled at the green.

00:58:05.190 --> 00:58:27.460
Then it was Vintage Palmer, not defending a one-stroke lead but on offense trying to increase it.

00:58:31.020 --> 00:58:33.060
for the fourth consecutive hole it was not

00:58:33.060 --> 00:58:36.530
to be. And so denied the

00:58:36.530 --> 00:58:38.560
